# mutgap2_res_mapper_texture_row_17: A one-component 8-bit IOSurface (L008, 16x4, one byte an element) with rows of 17 bytes, and a mapper-ref texture (type 11, R8Unorm 16x4, shader-read) over it: validateIOSurfaceDescriptor needs the surface's row bytes aligned to the device's IOSurface texture alignment, which 17 is not ("Invalid row byte alignment"), so creation fails and the exec that lists it faults; the probe slot stays zero. A texture over a surface with rows of 16 bytes is made and its exec runs. The IOSurface host device needs a memory map: map and isolate.
